            "description": "Bigg Boss Season 4 is the fourth installment of the Indian reality television show based on the Dutch series 'Big Brother,' which aired on Colors TV from October 3, 2010, to January 8, 2011. Hosted for the first time by Salman Khan, who went on to become the perennial host of the series, this season lasted 14 weeks or 97 days. The show features contestants, referred to as 'housemates,' living in a specially constructed house isolated from the outside world. They are constantly monitored by live cameras and personal audio microphones. Over the course of the show, contestants participate in various tasks and challenges and are voted out weekly by fellow participants and audiences, thereby leading to eliminations. The last remaining housemate is crowned the winner. The show was lauded for its high drama, interpersonal conflicts, and entertaining tasks, making it a highly rated season in Bigg Boss history. Contestants like Shweta Tiwari, Dolly Bindra, and Samir Soni played pivotal roles in the season's drama, while Shweta Tiwari emerged as the winner, becoming the first female winner in the franchise.",
